---
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import { githubStarsLabel } from "../github";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { GITHUB_URL, SELF_HOST_GUIDE_PATH, UPSTREAM_URL } from "../site";

const starsLabel = await githubStarsLabel();
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About · Matebot"
  description="Matebot is a self-hosted build of an open source Grok Bot alternative for persistent AI teammates."
>
  <div class="container">
    <Header starsLabel={starsLabel} />
    <main id="main" class="privacy-copy">
      <h1>About Matebot</h1>
      <p>
        Matebot is an open source Grok Bot alternative for persistent AI teammates: bots that can use a browser and shell,
        remember the work around a job, run routines on a schedule, and ask for approval when they reach a
        boundary. It is designed for practical operational work rather than one-off chat.
      </p>
      <h2>Why it exists</h2>
      <p>
        Useful agents should be understandable and controllable by the people who run them. Matebot keeps
        routines in readable Markdown, supports multiple model providers, records actions in an audit log, and
        lets operators keep model keys, browser sessions, and deployment infrastructure under their own
        control. The same bots and routines work across the web, desktop, and mobile clients.
      </p>
      <h2>Built on Rakazo</h2>
      <p>
        Matebot is our own branded deployment of <a href={UPSTREAM_URL}>Rakazo</a>, an Apache-2.0 project by
        Inbox Zero Inc. We run it on our own infrastructure, carry its licence and attribution, and keep our
        changes close to upstream so the work upstream does reaches this build. Bug reports about this
        deployment belong in <a href={GITHUB_URL}>this repository</a>; the upstream project handles its own.
      </p>
      <h2>Running it yourself</h2>
      <p>
        To run Matebot on your own infrastructure, start with the{" "}
        <a href={SELF_HOST_GUIDE_PATH}>self-hosting guide</a>. The source is on{" "}
        <a href={GITHUB_URL}>GitHub</a> under the Apache-2.0 license, and pull requests are welcome.
      </p>
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
